Appendix C: Actuator Polytope and Control Allocation

C.1 Actuator Force Bounds

The individual magnetic actuator forces are bounded:

0 \leq F_{M,f} \leq F_{Mf,\max}

0 \leq F_{M,r} \leq F_{Mr,\max}

C.2 Achievable Set

For a given total magnetic force F_M, the achievable set of pitch moments is

\mathcal{A}(F_M) = \left\{ M_M : M_M = x_{Mf} F_{M,f} + x_{Mr} F_{M,r} \right\}

subject to

F_{M,f} + F_{M,r} = F_M

0 \leq F_{M,f} \leq F_{Mf,\max}

0 \leq F_{M,r} \leq F_{Mr,\max}

C.3 Polytope Vertices

The set \mathcal{A}(F_M) is a line segment in the M_M space. Its endpoints occur at the actuator saturation boundaries.

Case 1: Front actuator saturated at maximum.

F_{M,f} = F_{Mf,\max}, \qquad F_{M,r} = F_M - F_{Mf,\max}

This requires F_M - F_{Mf,\max} \geq 0 and F_M - F_{Mf,\max} \leq F_{Mr,\max}. The pitch moment is

M_M^{(1)} = x_{Mf} F_{Mf,\max} + x_{Mr}(F_M - F_{Mf,\max})

Case 2: Rear actuator saturated at maximum.

F_{M,r} = F_{Mr,\max}, \qquad F_{M,f} = F_M - F_{Mr,\max}

This requires F_M - F_{Mr,\max} \geq 0 and F_M - F_{Mr,\max} \leq F_{Mf,\max}. The pitch moment is

M_M^{(2)} = x_{Mf}(F_M - F_{Mr,\max}) + x_{Mr} F_{Mr,\max}

Case 3: Front actuator at zero.

F_{M,f} = 0, \qquad F_{M,r} = F_M

This requires F_M \leq F_{Mr,\max}. The pitch moment is

M_M^{(3)} = x_{Mr} F_M

Case 4: Rear actuator at zero.

F_{M,r} = 0, \qquad F_{M,f} = F_M

This requires F_M \leq F_{Mf,\max}. The pitch moment is

M_M^{(4)} = x_{Mf} F_M

C.4 Achievable Interval

The achievable interval is

\mathcal{A}(F_M) = [M_M^{\rm low}, M_M^{\rm high}]

where

M_M^{\rm low} = \min(M_M^{(1)}, M_M^{(2)}, M_M^{(3)}, M_M^{(4)})

M_M^{\rm high} = \max(M_M^{(1)}, M_M^{(2)}, M_M^{(3)}, M_M^{(4)})

For typical parameters x_{Mf} < 0 < x_{Mr} and symmetric limits F_{Mf,\max} = F_{Mr,\max} = F_{M,\max}:

M_M^{\rm low} = x_{Mf} F_M \quad \text{(front actuator at max, rear at zero if } F_M \leq F_{M,\max}\text{)}

M_M^{\rm high} = x_{Mr} F_M \quad \text{(rear actuator at max, front at zero if } F_M \leq F_{M,\max}\text{)}

C.5 Allocation Feasibility

The combined feasibility condition is

\boxed{
\mathcal{A}(F_M) \cap \mathcal{S}(\lambda, a_x, F_{\min}) \neq \varnothing
}

This requires

\max(M_M^{\rm low}, M_M^{\min}) \leq \min(M_M^{\rm high}, M_M^{\max})

C.6 Control Allocation Quadratic Program

Given a desired total force F_M^{\rm des} and desired pitch moment M_M^{\rm des}, the allocation problem is

\min_{F_{M,f}, F_{M,r}} \left( w_1 (F_{M,f} + F_{M,r} - F_M^{\rm des})^2 + w_2 (x_{Mf} F_{M,f} + x_{Mr} F_{M,r} - M_M^{\rm des})^2 \right)

subject to

0 \leq F_{M,f} \leq F_{Mf,\max}

0 \leq F_{M,r} \leq F_{Mr,\max}

M_M^{\min} \leq x_{Mf} F_{M,f} + x_{Mr} F_{M,r} \leq M_M^{\max}

This is a quadratic program with linear constraints, solvable in real time.

