Appendix M: Proof of Proposition 2 (Decoupled Allocation)

M.1 Proposition Statement

Proposition 2 (Decoupled allocation). If x_{Mf} \neq x_{Mr}, the matrix

\mathbf{B} = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ x_{Mf} & x_{Mr} \end{bmatrix}

is invertible, and the individual actuator forces are

\begin{bmatrix} F_{M,f} \\ F_{M,r} \end{bmatrix} = \frac{1}{x_{Mr} - x_{Mf}} \begin{bmatrix} x_{Mr} & -1 \\ -x_{Mf} & 1 \end{bmatrix} \begin{bmatrix} F_M \\ M_M \end{bmatrix}

M.2 Proof

The determinant of \mathbf{B} is

\det(\mathbf{B}) = 1 \cdot x_{Mr} - 1 \cdot x_{Mf} = x_{Mr} - x_{Mf}

Since x_{Mf} \neq x_{Mr}, \det(\mathbf{B}) \neq 0, and \mathbf{B} is invertible.

The inverse of a 2 \times 2 matrix

\mathbf{B} = \begin{bmatrix} b_{11} & b_{12} \\ b_{21} & b_{22} \end{bmatrix}

is

\mathbf{B}^{-1} = \frac{1}{\det(\mathbf{B})} \begin{bmatrix} b_{22} & -b_{12} \\ -b_{21} & b_{11} \end{bmatrix}

Substituting:

\mathbf{B}^{-1} = \frac{1}{x_{Mr} - x_{Mf}} \begin{bmatrix} x_{Mr} & -1 \\ -x_{Mf} & 1 \end{bmatrix}

Therefore:

\begin{bmatrix} F_{M,f} \\ F_{M,r} \end{bmatrix} = \mathbf{B}^{-1} \begin{bmatrix} F_M \\ M_M \end{bmatrix}

as required. ∎

M.3 Polytope Constraint

The solution is valid only if the resulting actuator forces satisfy

0 \leq F_{M,f} \leq F_{Mf,\max}

0 \leq F_{M,r} \leq F_{Mr,\max}

This imposes the polytope constraint on the achievable (F_M, M_M) pairs.

